title: 'bridges relayer: resolve header hash by number without `chain_getBlockHash`'
doc:
- audience: Node Operator
  description: |-
    The relayer no longer requires `chain_getBlockHash` to resolve a block number to a hash.
    When the node doesn't answer it (light clients such as smoldot only answer for block zero),
    the relayer walks back through parent hashes from the best finalized header and caches every
    mapping on the way. The finality loop also stops downloading whole blocks when it only needs
    a header.
crates:
- name: relay-substrate-client
  bump: major
- name: finality-relay
  bump: minor
- name: substrate-relay-helper
  bump: patch
